{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation committed on branch `emb-2041` as `e655e1dc612` (Change-Id `I74bb67c3b73c6eabe85ae75c38bf5868be843a57`). `make verify` is running; Gerrit push follows.\n\n**What landed, against the plan's four properties.**\n\n*Vendor neutrality.* Both model choices are provider-qualified strings handed to pydantic-ai's own inference through two one-line seams, `_digest_model` (`infer_model`) and `_embedding_model` (`infer_embedding_model`). There is no vendor table to fall out of date, and adding a vendor is a configuration change. AC3 is enforced by an AST scan over `embedding.py`, `lexical.py` and `index.py` that fails if any of 8 vendor names appears inside an `If`, `IfExp`, `While` or `Compare` — the vendor list lives in the test, so the module cannot satisfy the rule by narrowing its own list.\n\n*Degrade, never fail.* `rank` returns `None` as the single degrade signal for all 5 unavailabilities (unconfigured, backend absent, provider denial, timeout, partial coverage); `find_similar` serves lexical. The distinction is in the logged diagnostic because no caller acts on it.\n\n*Full current-key coverage or nothing.* `validity_key` is sha256 over the embedding model and `DIGEST_PROMPT_COMMIT`, NUL-separated. Both the model change and the prompt-pin change invalidate; a partial corpus and an interrupted re-embed both degrade rather than rank across 2 spaces.\n\n*The create path pays nothing.* `catch_up` drops a rewritten document's vector rather than re-deriving it, so the build is the only thing that ever digests or embeds.\n\n**Three findings worth recording.**\n\n1. **The pinned prompt's source file no longer exists.** ADR 0122 pins the 4-field digest prompt at `f147e08242f`, but `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_digest.md` was deleted along with the whole overlap/enrich subsystem by an earlier complexity-reduction epic. The text was recovered with `git show f147e08242f:...` and vendored into `embedding.py` beside `DIGEST_PROMPT_COMMIT`, with a comment stating that editing the text without moving the pin would leave stored vectors describing text the digest no longer produces.\n\n2. **The cheap probe runs first, deliberately.** `_rank_or_raise` opens with `SELECT 1 FROM vectors LIMIT 1`. An install that never configured the tier is the common case and it runs on every create, so it must not pay a config-discovery pass and an import of the agents stack to be told \"not configured\".\n\n3. **A provider failure stops the build; a digest failure does not.** `_vector_one` raises `TierUnavailable` on a provider error so the run stops rather than burning one call per remaining ticket against an endpoint denying all of them. An unrecoverable digest is per-ticket: retried once, then counted and skipped.\n\n**Counter semantics as implemented.** `digest_unparsed` increments per unrecoverable reply (so a retried-then-successful ticket leaves it at 1 and `digest_failed` at 0); `digest_failed` only when both attempts fail; `empties` when a mapping *is* recovered but all 4 fields are empty, with no retry.\n\n**Two AC readings worth stating, since both could have been read the other way.**\n\n- **AC14** — all 3 of ADR 0122's reply shapes (`ticket_digest` wrapper, YAML, JSON behind a prose preamble) *recover* successfully. The test feeds all 3 carrying empty field values, so recovery succeeds 3 times and `empties == 3`. Reading them as unrecoverable would have tested the retry path instead.\n- **AC21** — \"create-path cost is flat in the unvectored share\" is about `catch_up`, not `find_similar`; a fully-covered query legitimately makes 1 query-embed call. Tested against `catch_up` at 0, 1 and 3 of 3 vectored: 0 provider calls in all three.\n\n**Test module.** 34 tests, all passing. The embedding provider is injected through the single `_embedding_model` seam using a deterministic bag-of-terms `EmbeddingModel` subclass, so cosine similarity is ordinary term overlap and the AC1 ordering assertion is a statement about the ordering rather than about a provider's weights. pydantic-ai's own `TestEmbeddingModel` could not be used: it returns all-1.0 vectors, so every pair is equidistant and no ordering is assertable.\n\nAC2 asserts real resolution for 2 distinct vendors (`BedrockEmbeddingModel`, `OpenAIEmbeddingModel`); AC11 asserts `cohere:embed-v4.0` degrades naming the optional group. AC4 uses the explicit `openai-chat:` prefix so the test does not depend on what a bare `openai:` will mean after pydantic-ai v2 changes its default.\n\n**Ratchets.** The mechanism gate initially reported 1 new entry — an autouse fixture clearing the 2 env vars. It was removed rather than justified: the 2 tests that need the unconfigured state now call `_unconfigure(monkeypatch)` explicitly, which both drops the mechanism and makes each test state its own precondition. Gate now exits 0 with no `new` or `increased`. `make lint` and `make typecheck` both pass; mypy is clean across 751 source files.\n\n**Not done here, per the plan:** exposing the build as a command or sweep is explicitly out of scope."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793619292709056602,"uuid":"ad5d75bd-12bf-46c2-8ec9-70edfc979719"}